WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.120
Good morning, John!

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:03.870
This is going to be my last video before I
go on paternity leave.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.580
John, I wouldn’t say that I’m addicted
to work.

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:07.590
I probably should.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:09.379
It’s gonna be weird to take a break.

00:00:09.379 --> 00:00:10.959
I don’t know what that’s gonna be like.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.579
I haven’t taken a break from doing this
in 10 years.

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:16.939
I started making YouTube videos when I was
26 years old. I'm 36!

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:18.640
Wow. Woah.

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:21.840
But in all honesty, I’m a little worried
about my ability to disengage.

00:00:21.849 --> 00:00:24.289
But before I leave you all, I have some housekeeping.

00:00:24.289 --> 00:00:26.729
I have made 2 videos that will upload during
paternity leave.

00:00:26.729 --> 00:00:28.800
I’ve already made them and uploaded them
and scheduled them.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:34.100
One is a promo video for VidCon that will
go up as soon as tickets go on sale in Australia,

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.360
Amsterdam, and the U.S.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.740
They’re already on sale in the U.S.; Australia
and Amsterdam will be coming soon.

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:42.320
Second, I will be on leave during Pizzamas,
which I feel bad about ‘cause the entire

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.480
idea of Pizzamas is that we make more videos
than usual, and I’m gonna miss it.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.160
So I made one and we’re having people cover
me for the other ones, but I wanted to talk

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:51.329
a little bit about Pizzamas this year ‘cause it’s
a little bit different in terms of our designs.

00:00:51.329 --> 00:00:53.930
This year, I decided to reach out to a bunch
of my favorite designers on the internet and

00:00:53.930 --> 00:01:00.140
ask them for their take on Pizza John, which
has resulted in a very diverse and weird group

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:03.120
of Pizza John designs that I’m very excited
about sharing with people.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.320
I’m wearing a Pizza John hoodie right now
that you can’t buy yet, which I shouldn’t even be showing you.

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:10.660
I’m also wearing a Pizza John design under
here ‘cause I was just making that video.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:12.260
But you’re not supposed to be seeing these
things at all.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.770
You’re not supposed to be seeing that this
hoodie has that thing.

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:15.370
Oh yeah.

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:16.570
These are all our test print run.

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:19.860
There’s a pile of Pizza John shirts behind
the camera staring at me, literally.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:23.620
But I’m very excited to unleash them upon
the world, and also I really like the video I made.

00:01:23.620 --> 00:01:24.340
So that’s VidCon and Pizzamas.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:26.260
Also, Project for Awesome is coming up.

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:30.229
I won’t be able to talk about that much
before the Project for Awesome happens, so

00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:33.789
get your Project for Awesomeing hands ready,
and if you don’t know what that is, you can Google it.

00:01:33.789 --> 00:01:35.309
John, maybe you want to make a video about
that.

00:01:35.309 --> 00:01:37.620
I know it’s probably my turn to do that.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:38.130
Sorry.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:42.370
I think last piece of housekeeping is that
I will be trying to disengage from social

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:44.000
media, which will be very hard for me.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.439
I’m gonna try to not tweet at all.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:49.530
There will be people tweeting as me—I think
mostly Victoria—just to let people know

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:52.850
about things that are happening, whether that’s
Project for Awesome or VidCon or Pizzamas

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:53.350
or whatever.

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:56.811
But I like creating content on my social media,
and there won’t be any of that because I’m

00:01:56.811 --> 00:01:58.191
gonna try my best not to do it.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.680
So I’ve scheduled some tweets for the future,
just so that there will be something coming out,

00:02:01.689 --> 00:02:02.810
and they’re hashtagged #pretweet.

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:07.750
But I can’t come up with six weeks worth
of tweets, so I’m asking you all to help me.

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:12.870
Leave down below ideas for things that you
would like me to tweet, and have them be about

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:18.280
120 characters so we can tag them and also
maybe tag you if you want to leave your Twitter handle there.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.000
And a weird thing happened to me today: I
got this in the mail.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.120
It’s a Google Pixel phone.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.600
Now I want to be clear: I’m an iPhone user.

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:29.840
I have no particular affinity for any kind
of phone, but they did send this to me because

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.280
it’s YouTube, it’s Google, and it’s
this related thing.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.160
I am gonna give this to my favorite tweet.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.490
It’s the XL version.

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:39.300
It’s got 128 gigabytes inside of it.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.030
I don’t know how they fit that many in there.

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:44.390
I don’t believe in upgrading a phone just
‘cause somebody sends you a $1000 phone,

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:45.810
so I’m gonna send it to one of you.

00:02:45.810 --> 00:02:46.480
Here it is.

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:47.280
I kissed it.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:50.640
So you gotta leave your Twitter handle so
that we can find you, and I’m gonna put

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:53.120
a hanklerfish on the back of this, so now
there’s that.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:55.590
And I bet whoever gets this is gonna need
it more than me.

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:56.920
And again, this is not a sponsorship.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.100
I do not endorse that phone.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.100
I know nothing about it.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:03.200
Choose whatever phone you would like to choose,
as long as it isn’t one of the explodey ones.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.420
And I think that’s it!

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:07.480
I think I’m gonna end this video, and then
I’m gonna go on paternity leave.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:09.940
It’s a thing that’s actually gonna happen.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:13.840
John, I’ll see you on Tuesday.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:16.420
You’ll see me whenever you come visit?

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.040
When’s that?

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:18.420
You coming to visit? You should do that.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:18.920
You should do that.

